What was taken, and what was not
--------------------------------
Taken (pattern and design lessons, re-implemented here; no upstream source file is copied verbatim):
- STEP-first generation: the model script is the tool, STEP is the primary artifact, and every output
  is content-hashed (sha256) so a rebuild can be checked.
- Determinism discipline (upstream `cadgen/_internal/determinism.py`): OCCT orders shapes by heap
  address, so anything that iterates a set of shapes must be re-ordered by content. Here that lesson
  is applied by building every face from an explicit, ordered vertex list and never iterating sets.
- Generators are plain Python with no network access, and a validator re-measures the files.

Not taken:
- The upstream kernel is build123d, not CadQuery. This fork uses CadQuery (as the MEP Co-pilot brief
  specifies), so none of the build123d / `cadgen` runtime, store, GLB/STL/3MF, kinematics or viewer
  code is included.

Everything under skills/cad/ other than LICENSE is MEP Co-pilot code. If any upstream source is
copied into this directory later, record the file and commit here.
